                    <msContents><!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>This inscription records an endowment to the Śaiva preceptor, Amr̥ta-rāśi-bhaṭṭāraka for the Nāgalēśvara temple in Taḻekallu in Śaka 913. The grant was made at Baṁkāpura. The major part of the grant is the 400 <foreign>mattar</foreign> of land. 
                            Many further details of the actual donation are lost as the inscription is damaged, however, the inscription does provide the details that this donation occurred during the reign of Taila II, when his subordinate Sōbhanarasa was ruling the “two six-hundreds” and the Banavāsi-12000. 
                            His subordinate, Sāviyaṇna was ruling the Kukkanūr-30 with his mercy. 
                        </summary>
                        <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
